            "topic": "Dora, Ufonia's AI clinical voice assistant, scales in the NHS and expands to the US",
            "summary": "Dora, built by Oxford-based Ufonia (the spoken text's 'Synphony' is a mis-transcription), phones patients to run routine clinical conversations such as post-cataract-surgery follow-ups, with 150,000+ autonomous consultations across ~15 NHS trusts. The company is now expanding into the US, with a full launch planned at ASCRS 2026; the '200,000 calls', '20 hospitals' and 'a million patients' figures could not be verified in two independent sources.",
